\details{
\subsection{PopulateObsCV}{

Expands a CV value to a named \verb{[nSim]} vector following the standard
\code{.StructurePars} + \code{ExtendSims} convention. If \code{CV} already has dimnames
(i.e. it has been previously populated), it is trimmed to \code{nSim} and
returned unchanged.
}

\subsection{PopulateObsError}{

Generates or validates a lognormal error array of dimension
\verb{[nSim x nYear]}.

If \code{object@Error} is empty and \code{object@CV} is set, draws \verb{nSim × nYear}
lognormal values with mean 1 and the specified CV, returning a named
\verb{[nSim x nYear]} array.

If \code{object@Error} is already provided, it is validated against the expected
dimensions. A pre-supplied array with more rows than \code{nSim} is silently
trimmed; mismatches in either dimension after trimming raise an error.
Dimension names are applied to the validated array before returning.
}

\subsection{PopulateObsBias}{

Expands a \code{Bias} value to a named \verb{[nSim]} multiplicative array on the
natural scale. Accepted inputs:
\itemize{
\item Empty or \code{NULL}: defaults silently to 1 (no bias).
\item Vector of length \code{nSim}: wrapped in a named array directly.
\item Vector longer than \code{nSim}: trimmed silently to \code{nSim}.
\item Scalar or length-2 vector: treated as a CV from which \code{nSim} lognormal
values are drawn.
}

All supplied values must be strictly positive.
}

\subsection{PopulateObsRef}{

Generates or returns a named \verb{[nSim]} reference level array. If \code{Ref} has
dimnames it is assumed already populated and trimmed to \code{nSim}. If
\code{length(Ref) == nSim} and \code{nSim != 2} (to avoid ambiguity with a length-2
uniform bound), it is returned as-is wrapped in a named array. Otherwise
\code{Ref} is treated as a CV and a lognormal draw of \code{nSim} values is taken.
}

\subsection{PopulateObsAC}{

Expands a lag-1 autocorrelation coefficient to a named \verb{[nSim]} array.
Accepted inputs:
\itemize{
\item Empty or \code{NULL}: defaults silently to 0 (no autocorrelation).
\item Scalar: constant value applied to all simulations.
\item Length-2 vector \code{c(lower, upper)} (when \code{nSim != 2}): bounds of a
Uniform distribution from which \code{nSim} values are drawn.
\item Vector of length \code{nSim}: used directly.
\item Vector longer than \code{nSim}: trimmed silently.
}

All values are validated to lie in \verb{[-1, 1]}.
}

\subsection{ApplyObsAC}{

Applies per-simulation lag-1 AR(1) autocorrelation to a
\verb{[nSim x nYear]} lognormal error array using a variance-preserving
formulation. Let \eqn{\varepsilon_t = \log(\mathrm{Error}_t)} be the
raw log-errors. The AR(1) series is constructed as:

\deqn{\varepsilon_t^* = \rho \, \varepsilon_{t-1}^* +
  \sqrt{1 - \rho^2} \, \varepsilon_t}

where \eqn{\rho} is the per-simulation autocorrelation coefficient. This
preserves the marginal variance \eqn{\mathrm{Var}(\varepsilon_t^*) =
\mathrm{Var}(\varepsilon_t)} for all values of \eqn{\rho}. The AR(1)
series is exponentiated back to the natural scale before returning. If all
AC values are zero the input array is returned unchanged.
}

\subsection{PopulateObsScalar}{

Expands a scalar, length-2 uniform bound, or named matrix to a
\verb{[nSim x nYear]} array, following the standard change-point convention
used throughout the operating model. Accepted inputs:
\itemize{
\item Named array with correct dimensions: trimmed to \code{nSim} and returned.
\item Length-2 vector \code{c(lower, upper)}: \code{nSim} values drawn from
\code{Uniform(lower, upper)}, held constant across years.
\item Scalar or change-point matrix: expanded via \code{.StructurePars} +
\code{ExtendSims} + \code{ExtendYears}.
}
}

\subsection{PopulateObsShift}{

Expands a \code{Shift} value to a named \verb{[nSim x nYear x nBin]} array following
the same change-point convention, with the third dimension named by
\code{BinName} and labelled with \code{Bins}. Accepted inputs:
\itemize{
\item Full \verb{[nSim x nYear x nBin]} array: trimmed to \code{nSim} if oversupplied.
\item Scalar: broadcast to all simulations, years, and bins.
